  "claim": "Marvin John Heemeyer the muffler repair shop owner inspired Mikhail Krichman film that Mikhail Krichman photographed.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Leviathan (2014 film). Sentence: According to Zvyagintsev, the story of Marvin Heemeyer in the United States inspired him and it was adapted into a Russian setting, but critics compare the story to the more similar biblical story of Naboth's Vineyard, where a King vies for his subjects' land and is motivated by his Queen to obtain it in a sly manner.\nPage: Marvin Heemeyer. Sentence: On June 4, 2004, automobile muffler repair shop owner Marvin John Heemeyer drove his armored bulldozer through Granby, Colorado, damaging 13 buildings, with the cost of the damage rounding to an estimated $7 million.\nPage: Mikhail Krichman. Sentence: He photographed all of Andrey Zvyagintsev's films, including \"The Return\" (2003), \"The Banishment\" (2007), \"Elena\" (2010) and \"Leviathan\" (2014).",
